## Why localhost did not work in Zscaler

The original preview ran at `http://127.0.0.1:8765/`. That address only works inside the browser or machine running the local server. A managed Zscaler browser is often isolated from that local server, so it cannot reach the app.

Publishing this repository with GitHub Pages gives the app a normal HTTPS URL:

`https://math100-pro.github.io/mathquest-academy/`

## GitHub Pages

This repo includes `.github/workflows/pages.yml`. After the repository is created, go to:

`Settings -> Pages -> Build and deployment`

Then choose `GitHub Actions` as the source. The workflow deploys the static app from the repository root.

## Prototype Storage

Accounts, password hashes, MP, streaks, premium status, and lesson progress are saved in browser `localStorage`. For production, use real backend authentication, a database, and Stripe webhooks before granting paid premium access
